# Hyperactivity for Chip Design: Complete Scope, Hyperfactored Two-Module Core, and the Maximum-Reflection Geodesic

## Abstract

Modern integrated-circuit design spends roughly 70% of its \$100M–\$500M non-recurring engineering budget and 2–4 year schedule reconciling disconnected representations of one physical system—architectural specifications, behavioral models, RTL, verification harnesses, gate netlists, static timing, physical placement/routing, SPICE transistor simulation, power/thermal/EM fields, optical lithography masks, and the software stack.

This document is the complete, self-contained specification and execution blueprint for unified chip design inside **Hyperactivity** (`docs/hyperactivity.hypercubical`, v32, §§1–11 and Appendices A–C). Three foundational conclusions govern the design:

1. **Nothing lives outside Hyperactivity (§1, §7.4, §9.4, §10.6, Appendix A).** Digital logic, tropical static timing, CMOS transistor duals, SPICE DAEs, Poisson electrostatic placement, 3D thermal/IR-drop PDEs, Maxwell electromagnetics, and Hopkins 2D-FFT inverse lithography are all native definitions inside Hyperactivity, compiled to frontier-speed C and GPU kernels. Univalence-driven layout/basis transport (`ua` + `transport`), topology specialization (`specialize`), coupled reverse-mode automatic differentiation, and proved incremental Schur/Woodbury derivatives make Hyperactivity frontier at *executing* physical solvers—not merely wrapping them.
2. **Hyperfactoring through existing `lib/` and `chem/` collapses the entire stack to TWO tiny bridge modules (~160 lines of new core) plus compact algebra tables.** Auditing the repository's existing 189 `lib/` modules and 75 `chem/` modules reveals that nearly every deep mathematical engine—fiber optimization (`in-fiber`/`in-fiber-key`), univalent vector/index transport (`vec-fin`, `package-transport`, `GraphSym`), semiring homomorphism folding (`SemiringOn`, `si-interp-hom`), polynomial normalization and forward AD (`ring.hypercubical`, `autodiff.hypercubical`), clocked guarded processes and choreographies (`GProc`, `Sim^κ`, `GChor`, `gproject`), credit conservation (`cr-conserved`), weak memory (`tso.hypercubical`, `rc11.hypercubical`), incremental maintenance (`Maintained`, `Derivative`, `se-maint`), cost-guided search (`navigate-by`, `best-by`), fraction-free Schur-complement elimination and Sylvester inertia (`chem/bareisswit.hypercubical`, `chem/sylvester.hypercubical`), coordinate-transported Laplacians (`chem/laplace.hypercubical`), and 24-line sum-of-squares certificate checking (`chem/sos.hypercubical`)—is **already built and checked**.
3. **Maximum internal reflection closes the loop on native cubical interaction-net silicon (§4.5).** Contextualizing the November 2026 breakout of interaction-net CPUs (Tendrils Compute's \$30M seed around Vine/Ivy and Architect Labs' Frostbite 7nm mesh at 4.59× perf/W), the geodesic culminates in Hyperactivity specifying, timing, placing, verifying, and emitting its own **GALS/asynchronous §4.5 cubical interaction-net tile**—directly attacking Frostbite's 41% global clock-tree energy wall, 800→500 MHz GDS wire cliff, 250% model-vs-RTL power error, and 800,000-line Lean 4 verification overhead.

