1. **Netlist-Specialized SPICE / Schur-Complement DAE Simulation:**
   * Legacy SPICE (Spectre, HSPICE, Xyce) dynamically interprets a netlist graph on every Newton–Raphson iteration, chasing CSR pointers and branching on device types.
   * Inside Hyperactivity, nonlinear BSIM DAEs ($C(v)\dot{v} + I(v) = u(t)$) compose with `chem/bareisswit.hypercubical`'s fraction-free Schur elimination and `chem/sylvester.hypercubical`'s inertia check. **Univalence (`ua`)** transports sparse matrices across CSR, BCSR, and hierarchical Schur blocks; **staged specialization (`lib/specialize.hypercubical`)** compiles the static netlist topology directly into straight-line, branch-free, register-blocked native C/CUDA code; `lib/maintenance.hypercubical`'s `Derivative` computes proved Woodbury/Schur rank-$k$ updates on local ECOs.
2. **Unitary-Fourier 2D DCT/FFT Engine for Both Electrostatic Placement & Inverse Lithography (OPC/ILT):**
   * Both **DREAMPlace-class analytical placement** ($\nabla^2 \phi = -\rho$ via 2D DCT/FFT + smooth LogSumExp/WA wirelength gradients) and **cuLitho-class Inverse Lithography / OPC** (Hopkins 2D-FFT aerial imaging + resist model + mask polygon optimization) are instances of Appendix A's unitary Fourier equivalence $\mathcal{F} : L^2 \simeq_{\text{unitary}} L^2$ (eq. A.3–A.5) paired with reverse-mode adjoint AD (§10.6).
